1. DEFINITIONS
--------------
"Charter" or "License" shall mean the terms, covenants, and conditions for use,
reproduction, and distribution set forth in this document.

"Licensor" shall mean the Haven Language Foundation and Lead Standards Architect
Anirudha Puthraya.

"Work" shall mean the Haven Programming Language runtime, compilers, virtual
machines, CLI tools, libraries, documentation, and ODCS/OFCS implementations
distributed under this License.

"Durable Record" shall mean a hardware-sealed, memory-immutable data structure
whose identity is cryptographically bound to an RFC 8785 canonical hash.

"Continuity Ledger" shall mean an append-only, tamper-evident Merkle write-ahead
ledger preserving execution transitions and operational intent.

"Zero Intent Loss (ZIL)" shall mean the architectural guarantee that valid user
actions and state mutations are sealed locally in durable storage before external
network acknowledgement.

"Living Intent Contract" shall mean a declared operational agreement defining
execution purpose, state invariants, and autonomic self-healing fallback policies.

"Universal Dimensional Safety" shall mean the first-class typing of physical and
financial units to guarantee dimensional correctness across scientific, financial,
and engineering computations.

