4. DIGITAL CONTINUITY & OPEN SOVEREIGNTY GUARANTEES
---------------------------------------------------
To ensure that all applications built with Haven remain faithful to the Open
Digital Continuity Standard, any distribution of Haven runtimes or derivative
execution platforms must uphold the following core principles:

  a) Local Sovereignty: The runtime must execute deterministically offline
     without requiring mandatory cloud connectivity, remote telemetry pings,
     or centralized licensing servers for core computation.

  b) Mathematical Integrity: Modifications to ledger mechanisms, durable
     records, or cryptographic verification algorithms must maintain or enhance
     tamper-evident auditability, Merkle proofs, and atomic state recovery.

  c) Zero Intent Loss: Applications handling critical state transitions must
     provide mechanisms to preserve user operational intent across unexpected
     power failures, crashes, or network partitions.

  d) Universal Interoperability: User data stored in continuity ledgers must
     remain exportable in documented, open formats with zero vendor lock-in.

