==============================================================================
A. ARCHITECTURAL GENESIS & SPECIFICATION OF HAVEN LANGUAGE
==============================================================================

Haven was engineered as the first general-purpose programming language designed
from foundational axioms for sovereign, disruption-tolerant computation.

Core Language Innovations:
  1. Natural Human Grammar: Clean English syntax eliminating cognitive fatigue:
     `set x to 42`, `remember KEY as "value"`, `increase count by 1`,
     `whenever condition:`, `otherwise if:`, `unless:`, `repeat N times:`.
  2. Hardware-Sealed Durable Records: `durable record` structures with zero
     in-place mutation and deterministic RFC 8785 SHA-256 canonical hashing.
  3. Native Functional Pipelines: Expressive data chaining via `|>` and `into`.
  4. Universal Living Intent Fabric (ULIF): Declared intent contracts with
     autonomic self-healing and instant Zero-Intent-Loss receipt minting.
  5. Universal Dimensional Safety: First-class physical and financial units
     preventing dimensional errors in science, finance, and engineering.
  6. Open Financial Continuity Standard (OFCS): Exact decimal monetary arithmetic,
     double-entry conservation invariants, and offline reconciliation.
  7. Autonomous Agent Mesh: Durable episodic memory ledgers for artificial
     intelligence agents and swarm consensus.

==============================================================================
B. UPSTREAM EXECUTION RUNTIME FOUNDATIONS & ACKNOWLEDGMENTS
==============================================================================

The Haven runtime virtual machine is built upon modern, high-performance
computational foundations. Underlying virtual machine execution primitives,
memory allocation mechanisms, and baseline C runtime structures are derived from
standard open-source runtime systems under the Python Software Foundation License
Agreement (PSF License v2, Copyright (c) 2001-2026 PSF; BeOpen.com; CNRI; CWI).

All grammar extensions, C parser modifications, durable memory record engines,
cryptographic Merkle continuity ledgers, natural language parsers, living intent
fabrics, dimensional safety systems, and ODCS/OFCS specifications are original
works authored and governed by Anirudha Puthraya and the Haven Language Foundation.

Official Haven Standards & Documentation: https://api.odcs.in
Source Repository: https://github.com/Veyra-Programming/haven-Language-
